"94_demovm.mst — A DEMO IN A VM OF ITS OWN (docs/process_services.md S6).

 The last thing the primary was still pumping. Every other VM in this system
 got its own thread and its own reasons to wake; a demo did not, because its
 60 Hz step ran as a string the host formatted and the primary's supervisor
 loop exec'd — `GamePane stepWithKeys: 4 mouseX: 100 y: 200 buttons: 1`,
 numbers baked into source, sixty times a second, on the user's LANGUAGE
 thread. A demo that hung hung the primary; a demo that crashed took the
 primary's world with it; and the supervisor loop was a frame pump wearing a
 supervisor's name.

 THREE THINGS HAD TO EXIST FIRST, and now all three do:
   * the frame clock — the process timer service (`Worker tickEvery:`), which
     wakes any VM at 60 Hz with no pump and no poll;
   * the pixels — the game command queue was ALWAYS process-global and
     main-drained, so a worker's GamePane commands reach the same Metal pane
     the primary's did. Nothing had to move; only the sink had to be installed
     in the demo's VM (`cocoa_gui/src/boot.rs`);
   * the input — `GamePane inputState` (prim 279), the read that replaced the
     formatted string, so a demo ASKS what the keyboard is doing instead of
     being told by whoever ran it.

 WHAT A DEMO STILL SHARES: one Metal pane, one at a time. That is a property
 of the pane (a single main-thread surface), not of the VM, and it is the
 reason this file has a `stopAll` rather than a fleet. Several demos at once
 is a pane question, not a threading one.

 THE SHAPE MIRRORS `93_appvm.mst` deliberately — a host on the primary that
 spawns and remembers, a client in the demo's VM that serves and ends itself.
 An app's frames cross as specs and blits; a demo's cross as GamePane commands
 through a queue that was already there. Same lifecycle, different payload."

"────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 IN THE DEMO'S OWN VM."
Object subclass: DemoVmClient [
    <classVars: Fps StartGen>

    "Installed by the init source `DemoVmHost` ships, AFTER the demo's own
     entry doit has run (so `GamePane onStep:` is already registered). From
     here the VM has exactly one job: step on the beat, and end when asked."
    DemoVmClient class >> serve [ ^self serveAt: 60 ]

    "TAKES NO ENTRY DOIT, on purpose. The obvious version passed the demo's
     launch source along so the client could report what it was running — and
     that meant embedding that source as a STRING LITERAL inside the init
     source, so any entry containing a quote (`Transcript showCr: ''hi''` —
     hardly exotic) produced malformed code in a fresh VM, where the failure is
     a worker that dies at birth. The entry runs before this and needs no
     second copy; introspection is not worth a quoting hazard."
    DemoVmClient class >> serveAt: n <Integer> [
        Fps := n max: 1.
        "WHICH STOP REQUESTS ARE OURS: the ones that come after we start. The
         first version read a sticky boolean, so a single earlier Escape made
         every later demo quit on its first beat — demos simply refused to
         open. Recorded before the tick is installed, so no beat can precede
         it."
        StartGen := GamePane exitGeneration.
        Worker onMessage: [ :m | DemoVmClient handle: m payload ].
        "THE FRAME CLOCK IS THE VM'S OWN. No supervisor, no host loop, no
         sleep: the timer service wakes this VM, the tick dispatches top-level
         like any other message, and the step runs one thing at a time exactly
         as everything else in this VM does."
        "OUR CLEANUP, ON EVERY EXIT ROUTE (Escape, the menu's Send exit, a
         relaunch, our own decision): the VM that opened the pane closes it.
         Wrapped here because `Worker exit:` cannot catch for us."
        Worker onExit: [
            [ GamePane new stop. GamePane reset ] on: Error do: [ :e | nil ] ].
        Worker onTick: [ DemoVmClient tick ].
        Worker tickEvery: 1000 // Fps.
        ^self
    ]

    "ONE FRAME. Errors are reported and swallowed rather than allowed to kill
     the VM: a demo that throws on frame 900 should say so and stop stepping,
     not vanish mid-animation leaving a frozen pane and no explanation. The
     tick is cancelled on the way out, because a broken step repeated sixty
     times a second is sixty identical traces a second."
    DemoVmClient class >> tick [
        "ESCAPE ENDS US, AND WE DO THE ENDING. The host does not kill a demo
         that has a VM of its own — it records the request with the rest of the
         input, and this notices on its very next beat and runs the same clean
         shutdown a menu stop runs. Checked BEFORE the step so the frame the
         user quit on is not drawn."
        GamePane exitGeneration > StartGen ifTrue: [ ^self shutdown ].
        ^[ GamePane stepFromInput ]
            on: Error do: [ :e |
                Worker tickEvery: 0.
                Transcript showCr: 'demo step failed: ' , e messageText.
                nil ]
    ]

    DemoVmClient class >> handle: payload <Object> [
        (payload isKindOf: Array) ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        (payload at: 1) == #demoExit ifTrue: [ ^self shutdown ].
        ^self
    ]

    "THE DEMO ENDS ITSELF (docs/process_services.md S5): stop the clock, let
     the demo drop its step block and its objects, announce, go. Called when
     the pane is dismissed — Escape, the close button, or another demo taking
     the screen."
    DemoVmClient class >> shutdown [
        "The pane is closed by the EXIT HOOK (installed in `serveAt:`), not
         here — so every route out does it, including the ones that never come
         through this method."
        Worker tickEvery: 0.
        ^Worker exit: #stopped
    ]

    DemoVmClient class >> fps ^ <Object> [ ^Fps ]
]

"────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ON THE PRIMARY — spawn, remember, and stop."
Object subclass: DemoVmHost [
    <classVars: Vms Watching>

    DemoVmHost class >> vms ^ <OrderedCollection> [
        Vms isNil ifTrue: [ Vms := OrderedCollection new ].
        ^Vms
    ]

    "Start `anEntry` (a demo's launch doit, e.g. 'Breakout launch') in a VM of
     its own. ONE AT A TIME, because one Metal pane: any demo already running
     is asked to end first, and its own exit tears the pane down."
    DemoVmHost class >> start: anEntry <String> ^ <Object> [
        | w |
        self watchExits.
        self stopAll.
        "GRANTED (S6): a demo may spawn its own compute workers —
         ParallelMandel is a shipped demo that does exactly that, and a demo
         that cannot use the machine's cores would be a downgrade from the
         in-process path it replaces."
        w := [ Worker spawnGranted: (self initSourceFor: anEntry) ]
            on: Error do: [ :e |
                Transcript showCr: 'demo: ' , e messageText.
                nil ].
        w isNil ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
        self vms add: w.
        "SAY SO. A demo that fails to appear with a silent transcript is
         undiagnosable from the user's chair — and S6's first live run was
         exactly that (a missing sink, every command a clean no-op). One line
         on launch means silence now has a meaning: launched-but-blank points
         at the pane, no line points at the spawn."
        Transcript showCr: 'demo: ' , anEntry , ' -> own VM'.
        ^w
    ]

    "Runs ONCE in the fresh VM: the demo's own entry doit exactly as the
     in-process path would run it, then the client that gives it a heartbeat.
     The entry is baked in rather than sent, so the demo is painting before
     anything else can arrive."
    DemoVmHost class >> initSourceFor: anEntry <String> ^ <String> [
        ^'[ ' , anEntry , '. DemoVmClient serve. ] value.'
    ]

    "Ask every demo VM to end. A message, not a kill: the demo stops its clock,
     resets the pane and announces its exit, which is what retires it here."
    DemoVmHost class >> stopAll [
        self vms do: [ :w |
            [ w send: (Array with: #demoExit) ] on: Error do: [ :e | nil ] ].
        ^self
    ]

    DemoVmHost class >> liveCount ^ <Integer> [
        | n |
        n := 0.
        self vms do: [ :w | w isAlive ifTrue: [ n := n + 1 ] ].
        ^n
    ]

    "A demo's own goodbye retires it (S5). The runtime's #workerDied arrives
     right after and finds nothing left, so one ending stays one line."
    DemoVmHost class >> watchExits [
        Watching == true ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        Watching := true.
        Worker alsoOnVmExiting: [ :goneId :why | DemoVmHost note: goneId ].
        Worker alsoOnWorkerDied: [ :deadId | DemoVmHost note: deadId ].
        ^self
    ]

    DemoVmHost class >> note: anId <Integer> [
        self vms copy do: [ :w |
            w id = anId ifTrue: [
                self vms remove: w ifAbsent: [ nil ].
                Transcript showCr: 'demo: stopped' ] ].
        ^self
    ]
]
